{"step_index":1389,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-25T23:04:33Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-25T18:04:33-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-25T18:04:37-05:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-25T18:04:33-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-25T18:04:37-05:00\nShowing lines 1-120 of 359\n1: \"\"\"Write output/SPEEDRUN_ROUTING_NOTES.md from mission_order.json, the scan logs and the self-check results.\"\"\"\r\n2: \r\n3: import argparse\r\n4: import json\r\n5: import sys\r\n6: from pathlib import Path\r\n7: \r\n8: from validate_final import check_json, check_mermaid\r\n9: \r\n10: LANGUAGE_TABLE_OFFSETS = [\"0x19be000\", \"0x2458000\", \"0x2f2c000\", \"0x3a0e000\", \"0x44b3000\", \"0x4f8f000\", \"0x5a1a000\",\r\n11:                           \"0x644b000\", \"0x6f5a000\", \"0x7a24000\", \"0x84eb000\", \"0x9041000\", \"0x9b7e000\"]\r\n12: AUTOLAUNCH_MARKERS = (\"AUTOLAUNCH\", \"AUTO-LAUNCH\")\r\n13: \r\n14: INTRO = \"\"\"# Speedrun routing notes: main story, build 1.0.2.1 (Xbox dump)\r\n15: \r\n16: Everything below comes from files in the dump or from the decompiled scripts in `americas_scripts_23_11_2026`.\r\n17: Each claim is marked **observed** (read directly from data or code) or **inferred** (a conclusion drawn from\r\n18: observed facts). Anything not recovered is listed under \"Not recovered\" and is `null` in the JSON.\r\n19: \r\n20: ## What was and was not recovered\r\n21: \r\n22: - **Titles: recovered.** {titled} of {total} entries have their in-game English title.\r\n23: - **Mission order: recovered as stored order.** The game ships its own ordered mission list ({story_count} entries).\r\n24:   The flowchart follows it.\r\n25: - **Prerequisite edges: not recovered.** No data field and no script check was found that gates one mission on\r\n26:   another. `prerequisites`, `unlocks` and `is_bottleneck` are therefore `null`, and the arrows in the flowchart mean\r\n27:   \"next in the game's list\", not \"unlocks\".\r\n28: - **Protagonist per mission: recovered for {protagonist_count} main-story entries** from a required-player property\r\n29:   on the mission trigger records.\r\n30: - **Any% skips: {auto_count} main-story entries and {auto_side_count} side entries** are flagged by the game itself\r\n31:   rather than \n<truncated 3707 bytes>\ns toward 100% completion, or start a new game.\" No edge from a finale to `INT_CRED` was found, so none is\r\n87: drawn.\r\n88: \"\"\"\r\n89: \r\n90: PHASE3_HEAD = \"\"\"## Phase 3: order, branches, protagonists, skips\r\n91: \r\n92: ### Flag store (`Virtual.type_37658EE3464E5234`)\r\n93: \r\n94: **Observed.** All 31 call sites were read. `Method_0` adds an ID, `Method_1` tests for an ID. No `Method_1` result\r\n95: gates enabling or launching another mission. The readers are: the \"already added\" test before `Method_0` in three\r\n96: wrappers of `0x947D998BD81F7AC1`, the tests inside `func_10AA55`, and `func_10AD05`. `story000.ysc.cs` has no call\r\n97: to this type. So this store yields no prerequisite edges.\r\n98: \r\n99: ### Auto-flags in `func_10AA55` (controller `0xD2601E252151E04B.ysc.cs`, lines 572807-573097)\r\n100: \r\n101: **Observed.** The function receives a mission ID. For specific IDs it adds other IDs to the flag store.\r\n102: \r\n103: **Inferred.** The function has no direct caller and sits next to the store's add hook, so it most likely runs when\r\n104: the ID is added to the store (mission completion), not when the mission starts. The request described it as\r\n105: \"when the mission starts\"; the code does not show that.\r\n106: \r\n107: {auto_table}\r\n108: \r\n109: **Inferred for routing.** Because the game sets these flags itself, the flagged missions do not have to be played\r\n110: before the triggering mission. They are marked `any_percent_required: false`. Every other mission is `null`\r\n111: (unknown), not `true`: nothing proves that the remaining missions are all mandatory.\r\n112: \r\n113: When the ID is `BIL_FINAL_B` (line 572926) or `BIL_FINALE_M` (line 572935) the function calls\r\n114: `_0x58BECE7D02A750A7(0x4EF9B888, -1, 1, -1)` instead.\r\n115: \"\"\"\r\n116: \r\n117: ORDER_TEXT = \"\"\"### Stored mission order\r\n118: \r\n119: **Observed.** `story000.rpf` @ 0x3e30b5000, list key 0xB95219D4, holds {story_count} IDs in a fixed order.\r\n120: {main_sequence_count} of them are main-story entries by the prefix rule. The replay menu (`data.rpf` @ 0x12010000)\r","truncated_fields":["content"]}
